  'how.title': 'How does it work?',
  'how.source': 'Source',
  'how.chat.1': 'A turn runs these stages in order: ensure, compaction (skipped: the Lab never compacts), flush_decision, flush, reindex, recall, prompt, stream, persist.',
  'how.chat.2': 'The flush decision comes before the main run (upstream order, D1). When triggered, the flush turn writes only to today\'s daily file; bootstrap files are read-only.',
  'how.chat.3': 'Auto-recall is demo-only: memory_search runs on the user message; only MEMORY.md and today\'s/yesterday\'s daily file reach the prompt. Off for subagent/cron and reset turns.',
  'how.chat.4': 'The transcript window is demo-only: last 40 messages, 24,000 chars.',
  'how.chat.5': 'The tool loop is the Lab\'s (host): memory_search, memory_get (upstream definitions) and the curation tools; at most 6 tool rounds plus 1 final round without tools. Curated writes are an extension (Q16, D5) with per-target flags.',
  'how.chat.6': 'Without a key the chat answers 400 no_api_key; there is no fake model.',
  'how.chat.7': '/new and /reset run the session-memory hook (memory/<date>-<HHMM>.md, raw lines, no redactor, D2) and start a new session; a bare command sends the reset prompt in its own turn.',
  'how.chat.src': 'docs/lab.md › A chat turn · What is real, what is not',
  'how.heartbeat.1': 'Runtime-only port: no scheduler; the heartbeat runs by hand.',
  'how.heartbeat.2': 'The virtual clock is demo-only: it shifts the due checks only.',
  'how.heartbeat.3': 'A run streams the flush decision first, then either a skip (skipped) or the prompt, tool calls, the reply and the decision.',
  'how.heartbeat.4': 'The reply parser (/heartbeat/strip) checks text only and returns {shouldSkip, text, didStrip}.',
  'how.heartbeat.src': 'docs/lab.md › What is real, what is not · Endpoints',
